{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>The song, etc.</b> The kaf is for נכח (toward) Judah." "<b>כליל התקדש חג.</b> (A night sanctified as a festival) — the night of Passover. Therefore the early ones of blessed memory said that on the night of Passover the camp of Assyria was wiped out." "<b>לבא בהר יי.</b> (To come to the mountain of YHWH) — a matter like its parallel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:08.775893232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}